{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And from fifty years of age he shall return.</b> Each one <b>from the labor of service</b> imposed upon him: the Kohathites from the labor of carrying on the shoulder, and the Gershonites and Merarites from loading and unloading and lowering and raising, and both these and those return to song and to guarding, that no outsider enter the Tabernacle." "<b>And he shall no longer serve.</b> Rashi explained: the labor of carrying on the shoulder. According to Rashi, this verse does not refer to the sons of Gershon and Merari. And it is difficult for me regarding Rashi's interpretation, from itself, for he explained 'but he returns to load wagons' — what is he returning to? Was their service from the outset to load wagons? Nevertheless, the sons of Gershon and Merari are also disqualified at fifty from what they had been doing already, such as loading and unloading wagons and lowering and raising the Tabernacle, and they return to song and to guarding, that no outsider enter the Tabernacle. And according to Rashi's interpretation, that he explained 'but he returns to locking gates and to song and to loading wagons' — 'locking gates' refers to Shiloh and the Eternal House, and 'loading wagons' refers to the wilderness."], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :register {:flags {1 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {1 "The text cites Rashi by the abbreviated form פירש״י / פרש״י, rendered here as 'Rashi' following the standard convention for this commentator. The parenthetical 'but he returns…' quotes Rashi's words on this verse."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:17:06.732389831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}